{
  "message": "I've drawn a cited-answer assistant on AWS for this test. SharePoint and Confluence feed a small keyword-search catalog through the local test servers, staff use a sign-in-protected web app, and Teams is a note for later; Sydney is only a suggested region, not an approved one. The next missing decision is the model: which Amazon Bedrock model ID should we use, and is it already enabled in your account? \"Not sure\" is fine.",
  "phase": "Architecture",
  "proposal": {
    "baseRevision": 1,
    "title": "AWS bounded keyword RAG knowledge assistant (qualification design)",
    "body": "Scope: a web app with Cognito sign-in (PKCE and MFA) calls an IAM/JWT-protected HTTP API. The API calls a bounded keyword-RAG Lambda, which reads a DynamoDB catalog and calls an existing Bedrock model to produce cited answers. SharePoint and Confluence are existing external systems, reached only through the approved local normalized source-contract test servers. This does not verify native vendor APIs, real tenants, group expansion or inherited permissions, so production stays blocked. Teams is deferred and shown as a note. Assumptions: keyword retrieval, not vector search; up to 100 small UTF-8 documents. The region is unselected (Sydney ap-southeast-2 is only a candidate), and the model ID, quotas and availability are unverified. Nothing is deployed.",
    "next": {
      "version": 1,
      "revision": 1,
      "name": "AWS knowledge assistant (SharePoint/Confluence, cited answers)",
      "provider": "aws",
      "requirements": "Cited answers from approved SharePoint/Confluence documents through a web app. Preserve permissions, updates and deletes. Include recovery and audit. Teams comes later.",
